BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NAMI Night at South Burlington Public Library
DTSTART:20261104T180000
DTEND:20261104T193000
DTSTAMP:20261104T184252Z
UID:c9ecfb9777158f4983af3e3fac9b69@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:NAMI Vermont is partnering with South Burlington Public Librar
 y once again to bring a FREE mental health outreach presentation to the co
 mmunity! Join us on November 4th\, from 6:00- 7:30 p.m.\, for a night of l
 earning and connection. Our trained volunteer presenters will share their 
 mental health experiences to raise awareness about the impact of mental he
 alth conditions\, challenge harmful stereotypes about mental health\, and 
 inspire hope and healing. This is a safe space where participants can ask 
 questions\, talk about their own experiences\, and learn more about local 
 resources. This event is open to the public\, with no registration needed.
  Feel free to share this opportunity with a close friend\, family member\,
  or co-worker who may be interested in learning more about mental health. 
 We hope to see you there!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:South Burlington Library\, 180 Market St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/nami-night
 -at-south-burlington-public-library-09-10-2026-11-28-01
END:VEVENT
